    "durationMs": 126137,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. \n\n**What I built:**\n- **`app/`** — FastAPI 0.115 with async SQLAlchemy 2.0 + psycopg 3: `POST /links` (auto or custom codes, 201/409/422), `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` (atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING` for exactly-once click counting, 302 redirect), `GET /links` (creation-order list with total). Custom handlers ensure 404/409/422 responses all carry an `error` field, and URLs are stored/returned byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- **`alembic/`** — migration `0001` creates the `links` table with a unique indexed code column; `alembic/env.py` reads `DATABASE_URL` (nothing hard-coded).\n- **`start.sh`** — executable; runs `alembic upgrade head` then serves via uvicorn on `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground.\n- **`requirements.txt`** — pinned to the preinstalled versions; **`README.md`** — startup instructions.\n\n**Verification results** (against the live postgres at `postgres:5432`):\n- All 50+ smoke checks passed: URL/code validation (boundary lengths 4/20, charset, non-ASCII rejected), malformed JSON → 422, duplicates → 409, redirects increment exactly once, list ordering/total.\n- Killed and restarted the server via `sh start.sh`: click counts and all data survived, and re-running migrations was a clean no-op.\n- Stopped the test server and truncated my test rows, so the grader starts with an empty table and a single alembic head."
